{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The hand of the LORD came down on me [Eb]and set me in a val[Bb]ley wide
And it was full of bones, very ma[Eb]ny, very [Bb]dry
He led me all around them and he [Eb]asked me can they [Gm]rise
Son of [F]man, can these [Eb]bones live
O Lord GOD, you [Bb]know
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Dry bones, hear the [Eb]word of the LORD
I am going to put breath in [Bb]you, and you will live
Dry bones, hear the [Eb]word of the LORD
And you will know that [Bb]I am the LORD
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
So I prophesied as I was [Eb]commanded
And there was a [Bb]sound, a rattling
And the bones came to[Eb]gether, bone to [Gm][F]bone
Sinews on them, [Eb]flesh had grown, and skin had covered them o[Bb]ver
But there was no breath in them
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Dry bones, hear [Eb]the word of the LORD
I am going to put breath [Bb]in you, and you will live
Dry bones, hear the [Eb]word of the LORD
And you will know that [Bb]I am the [Eb]LORD
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Come from the [Bb]four [Gm]winds, O breath
[F]And breathe into these [Eb]slain, that they [Bb]may live
The breath came [F]into [Eb]them
They came to [Bb]life and stood on [Gm]their feet
[F]Our bones are dried [Eb]up, our hope is gone
I am going to open your graves
I will put my Spirit in you, and you [Bb]will live
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Dry bones, hear the word of the [Eb]LORD
I am going to put breath in [Bb]you, and you will live
Dry bones, hear the [Eb]word of the LORD
And you will know that [Bb]I am the [Eb]LORD
